.TH mnnn-schedule 1  "mnnn-schedule 2.23.0" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mnnn\-schedule \- Schedules: run a rule set (or, from 2.26, an ingest connector) at start_at, every interval or at cron times, until ends_at
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmnnn schedule\fR [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-\-db\fR] [\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-\-log\-file\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR] [\fB\-\-transport\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Schedules: run a rule set (or, from 2.26, an ingest connector) at start_at, every interval or at cron times, until ends_at
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Muninn home directory (default ~/.muninn)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_HOME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-db\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Database file (default <home>/storage/muninn.database)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_DB\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR
Never prompt; missing values are errors
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_NON_INTERACTIVE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
More output (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-file\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Write logs to this file instead of stderr (the TUI defaults to <home>/logs/tui.log)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_LOG_FILE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print nothing but errors and requested data
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_QUIET\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Answer yes to every confirmation
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_YES\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR \fI<THEME_MODE>\fR
Override the theme mode for this run
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
light
.IP \(bu 2
dark
.IP \(bu 2
system
.RE
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_THEME_MODE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-transport\fR \fI<stream|poll>\fR
How live collaboration reaches peers: `stream` (gRPC streams, the default) or `poll` (requests over the peer connection; for containers). Overrides MUNINN_COLLAB_TRANSPORT and the `net config \-\-collab\-transport` setting
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH NOTES
.PP
Timing:
  run_every   an interval: date items (2 hours 30 minutes, 1 month, 1 year), short codes
              (ms s m h d w M y: 90m, 1h30m, 2w, 1M), milliseconds (5000), or `once`.
              Times (tomorrow, 9am, next monday) go in \-\-start\-at.
  \-\-cron      instead of run_every: "0 9 * * 1\-5" (minute hour day month weekday), in \-\-tz.
  \-\-start\-at  when the first run is due (GNU date style: "tomorrow 9am", "2026\-12\-01 08:00",
              "next monday 06:00", "+2 hours"). None: right away (run_every) or the next cron time.
  \-\-ends\-at   no run starts at or after it. \-\-for 2w: ends_at = start + 2 weeks.
  \-\-tz        the zone dates are read and months/cron step in (UTC when not given; `local`).
  once        one run at \-\-start\-at (ends_at = start_at + 1 ms). Missed, it is skipped:
              one failed `missed` run, then disabled (history kept).
A past \-\-start\-at asks: the next interval, or a corrected start (a one\-off can only be
corrected). Without a terminal give \-\-past next\-interval.
.PP
Examples:
  mnnn schedule add nightly \-\-ruleset Cleanup "1 day" \-\-start\-at "tomorrow 02:00" \-\-tz local
  mnnn schedule add weekdays \-\-ruleset Report \-\-cron "0 9 * * 1\-5" \-\-tz Europe/Oslo
  mnnn schedule add reminder \-\-ruleset Notes once \-\-start\-at "2026\-12\-01 09:00"
  mnnn schedule parse "1h30m" \-\-start\-at "next monday 9am"
  mnnn scheduler run          # keep running (or let the TUI / org host do it)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
